DESCRIPTION="C5 — massive concurrency: PRODUCER_CLIENTS concurrent producer connections in closed loop (each client sends its next event as soon as the previous one commits), spread over PRODUCER_REPLICAS pgbench containers and multiplexed by PgBouncer (transaction pooling, PGBOUNCER_PROCESSES × PGBOUNCER_POOL_SIZE server connections), plus business readers. Millions of events per run; producer latency includes the wait for a pooled server connection. Labels: a; b (LOCK_SLOTS=1024, 16 slots per server connection; BEGIN / FOR SHARE / INSERT / COMMIT holds a pooled connection for 4 round trips); b-1rt (single-statement routing, producer-1rt.sql: 1 round trip); b-slots64 (64 slots: several pooled connections per controller row)."
